              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "31822583"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Phosphatase with activity against multiple substrates (PubMed:31822583). Acts as a metabolite repair enzyme which eliminates toxic glycolytic side products (PubMed:31822583). Dephosphorylates 2-phosphoglycolate which is generated during the repair of oxidative DNA lesions (By similarity). Dephosphorylates 4-phosphoerythronate, a side product which is produced by GAPDH and which inhibits 6-phosphogluconate dehydrogenase (PubMed:31822583). Dephosphorylation of 4-phosphoerythronate prevents the accumulation of high 4-phosphoerythronate levels which would otherwise inhibit the pentose phosphate pathway (PubMed:31822583). Dephosphorylates 2-phospholactate which may be a product of the methylglyoxal pathway (PubMed:31822583)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
